Mother lifted an edge of a tea towel that pasties were covered with, took one pasty and slowly started to chew. It seemed to her that stuffing had a strange smack. She stopped to chew for a second but pasty was delicious and well baked through so she finished it.
Soon she felt stomach ache. As far as she didn't eat anything that day, pasties were under suspicion. She shook them out of the basket under the bush and rushed to Grandmother whose hut was already not far. Making a few forced stops  on her way she finally reached the forest edge.